# The log of the test must have a line for each of these patterns (grep -E). A line with "!" at the start is a
# pattern that the log must not have.
# The player is in front of the mirror that faces the y direction. The picture has the view of the player and the
# frame of the mirror. The player counts as drawn, because the mirror shows the player.
\[3\.50\].* dump JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(-95 -3110 109\) .* lastRendered=0\.0 
\[3\.50\].* visible frames=2 surfaces=63 
# The faucet of the bathroom is in view. The faucet of the kitchen is behind the wall of the mirror, and the frame of
# the mirror does not have it.
\[3\.50\].* dump Faucet1 .* loc=\(-100 -3020 121\) .* lastRendered=0\.0 
\[3\.50\].* dump Faucet0 .* loc=\(-89 -2980 117\) 
!\[3\.50\].* dump Faucet0 .* lastRendered=0\.0 
# The player is in front of the mirror that faces the x direction, and that mirror shows the player also.
\[5\.50\].* dump JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(1830 -1150 109\) .* lastRendered=0\.0 
\[5\.50\].* visible frames=2 surfaces=66 
